---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Gabrielle",
  servesCuisine: ["Southern", "American"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-843-990-5460",
  url: "https://hotelbennett.com/dining-and-lounges/gabrielle",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "404 King Street",
    addressLocality: "Charleston",
    addressRegion: "SC",
    postalCode: "29403",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Gabrielle at Hotel Bennett, Charleston — executive chef Edgar Kano's \"Stylishly Southern\" restaurant opening onto Marion Square, serving breakfast, lunch, dinner, and weekend brunch.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gabrielle Menu Guide (2026) — Hotel Bennett, Charleston | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to Gabrielle at Hotel Bennett, Charleston: hours, signature dishes, official menu prices (Feb 2024 era), and reservations."
  path="/gabrielle-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/gabrielle-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/gabrielle-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a chic French brasserie dining room with rattan chairs, marble tables and tall windows in daylight (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Charleston, SC
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Gabrielle — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Gabrielle is the flagship restaurant of <strong>Hotel Bennett</strong> at 404
      King Street — the hotel's own term for the cooking is <strong>"Stylishly
      Southern,"</strong> and the restaurant claims the distinction of being
      Charleston's only restaurant opening directly onto Marion Square. Executive
      chef <strong>Edgar Kano</strong> leads the kitchen (with pastry chef Rémy
      Fünfrock), serving breakfast, lunch, dinner, and weekend brunch. Unlike most
      of its peers, Gabrielle's official menu PDFs carry real prices — but note the
      era: the latest official dinner menu is <strong>February 2024</strong>, so call
      ahead to confirm. Everything is written in our own words.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">404 King St, Charleston, SC 29403 (Hotel Bennett, on Marion Square)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive chef Edgar Kano; pastry chef Rémy Fünfrock</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">"Stylishly Southern" (hotel's own term)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">$$$$ — official Feb 2024 dinner PDF: steaks $58–$70</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Resy (bookable) or 843-990-5460</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Recognition</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">2024 OpenTable Diners' Choice (per Charleston Living Magazine)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Per the official Hotel Bennett dining page, crawled ~Sep 2026:
        <strong>breakfast daily 7:00–10:30 AM; lunch daily 11:30 AM–3:00 PM;
        dinner daily 5:00–10:00 PM; brunch Saturday–Sunday 11:30 AM–3:00 PM.</strong>
        The lounge and plaza run Sun–Thu 11 AM–11 PM and Fri–Sat 11 AM–midnight,
        with live music Friday–Saturday 6–9 PM.
      </p>

      <h2>Signature dishes</h2>
      <p>
        The press-verified signatures:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bigeye tuna tiradito</strong>: with kombu-chile ponzu.</li>
        <li><strong>King's Tower</strong>: the seafood tower — $200 on the official breakfast-era menu.</li>
        <li><strong>Hotel Bennett Royal Ossetra caviar</strong>: 30g $100 / 50g $160 (official menu).</li>
        <li><strong>Eggs Bennett</strong>: $39 — the namesake breakfast plate.</li>
        <li><strong>Seared golden tilefish</strong>: in lemon beurre blanc (Charleston Magazine).</li>
        <li><strong>She-crab soup</strong> and <strong>mushroom pasta</strong>: the Southern comfort anchors.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official prices (February 2024 era)</h2>
      <p>
        These are the restaurant's own figures from its official menu PDFs —
        <strong>February 2024 era, not 2026</strong>. Confirm current pricing before
        visiting:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dinner:</strong> 16oz boneless ribeye $70; 8oz filet mignon $62; 14oz veal chop $62; red wine braised short ribs $58.</li>
        <li><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Eggs Bennett $39; avocado toast $24; buttermilk waffle $19; brioche French toast $19; Bennett Continental $20.</li>
        <li><strong>From the Oct 2023 dinner menu:</strong> citrus-crusted Maine scallops $42; Pommery-crusted Australian rack of lamb $55; sides $12–14.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one dinner here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start with:</strong> the bigeye tuna tiradito — it's the dish the press keeps naming.</li>
        <li><strong>The splurge:</strong> the King's Tower or the ossetra caviar for the full Marion Square occasion.</li>
        <li><strong>The steak play:</strong> the 16oz ribeye (reported $70, Feb 2024 era).</li>
        <li><strong>Brunch:</strong> the Eggs Bennett — it's the namesake for a reason.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book on Resy</strong> — the venue page is live and bookable — or call 843-990-5460.</li>
        <li><strong>Prices are 2024-era:</strong> the official menu PDFs date to February 2024; ask about current pricing when you book.</li>
        <li><strong>Marion Square:</strong> the hotel's own claim is that Gabrielle is the only restaurant opening onto the square — ask for a square-facing table.</li>
        <li><strong>Weekend brunch</strong> runs 11:30 AM–3:00 PM Saturday and Sunday.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://hotelbennett.com/dining-and-lounges/gabrielle" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — Gabrielle at Hotel Bennett</a> (hours, events)</li>
        <li><a href="https://resy.com/cities/charleston-sc/venues/gabrielle-at-hotel-bennett" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reservations on Resy</a> (bookable; or call 843-990-5460)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.hotelbennett.com/pdf/Gab Dinner 2.24.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official dinner menu (PDF, Feb 2024 era)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        The figures above are <strong>official — but February 2024 era</strong>,
        from the restaurant's own menu PDFs hosted on hotelbennett.com. They are
        the latest official published prices we could verify, but they are not
        2026 prices. Always verify with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More South Carolina guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-south-carolina/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in South Carolina →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/iron-rose-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Iron Rose</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Southern coastal at Mills House</span></li>
        <li><a href="/frannie-and-the-fox-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Frannie &amp; The Fox</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— wood-fired Italian at The Emeline</span></li>
        <li><a href="/palmetto-cafe-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The Palmetto Cafe</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Lowcountry dining at The Charleston Place</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
